  "comments": "1992 saw the changeover from bronze to copper-plated steel for both the 1p &amp; 2p to reduce the cost of production. Both bronze and copper-plated steel 1992 coins can be found, however those in Proof &amp; Brilliant Uncirculated sets were struck in Bronze, while circulation strikes were copper-plated steel.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">1993 reverse die varieties:</span><br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Reverse A</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(1992-93)</span> P shorter foot, E between pearls, pearls near to border;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Reverse B</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(1993-97)</span> P longer foot, E at a pearl, pearls far from border;<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5df211fcdbde7.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5df211fcdbde7.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nInformation has been received to suggest that 1993 BU and Proof sets were struck with Reverse B but this is yet to be confirmed.",
